imaging (MRI) showed mild cerebellar atrophy (Fig. 1A). In
1998, she complained of severe trunk stiffness with board-like
rigidity of the abdomen and painful muscle spasms, but there
was no rigidity of the extremities. In 2000, she suffered polyuria and dry mouth. DMwas diagnosed because of her high
fast blood glucose and glycosylated hemoglobin Alc (Hb Alc)
