GABA-nergicneuron that acts as an inhibitory neuron in the

central nervous system. Up to 30% of patients with SPS have
IDDMand up to 65% of SPS patients also have antibodies
against GAD-65 and GAD-67 ( 1 , 8). Anti-GAD-Abs are present
in patients with SPS as well as in IDDMpatients, but their
titers in SPS are markedly higher than in IDDM. Anti-GADAbs in SPS inhibit the synthesis of GABAand recognize both
the conformational and denatured forms of GAD(1 , 7, 8). These
findings support the speculation that there is a difference in the
epitope of GADin the two diseases.
